// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27f/ui_targets.t27 -- the plan for the T27 OS UI on three targets from one object model.
; Issue t27#13294, epics t27#11037 (T27 OS) and t27#10782 (the 27-petal menu from one t27 spec).
; --
; Owner order 2026-11-08: the T27 OS UI runs on three targets -- the browser (t27b opens a site), the
; native desktop window, and the AX7203 framebuffer -- all drawn from one object model. First the
; 27-petal menu on all three, then the UI Kit. Zero hand layout: every pixel comes from VfGraph +
; VcStyle + tokens, and a target only maps one display list to its device.
; --
; This file is the plan, not a second model. It defines no graph, no style, no token and no display
; list; it names the spec that owns each object and each arrow of the data flow, and labels each one:
;   EXACT     the owner spec on master defines it and tests it;
;   DERIVED   master has a form of it, but not the one the plan needs (the gap column says what differs);
;   MISSING   master has no spec for it; the PR column names the open PR that holds a piece, 0 for none.
; A row whose piece sits in an open PR is never EXACT: an open PR is not master.
; --
; The data flow, one arrow per row of UT_ARR_*:
;   menu  --A0-->  graph   --A2-->  layout  --A6-->  display list  --A8-->  browser
;   label --A1-------------------------------------->  display list  --A9-->  desktop
;   frame --A3-->  layout                               display list  --A10-> fpga
;   glass --A4-->  tokens  --A5-->  style   --A7-->  display list
; Read on master 28fd63d1c0 (2026-11-08):
;   - VfGraph (visual_factory_contract.t27) has 8 kinds and no petal quad kind, and holds 16 nodes;
;     the menu needs 29 (a root, the centre, 27 petals). vf_layout.t27 keeps [16] arrays, and that
;     file is changed by open PR 13254, so raising the cap waits on it.
;   - VcStyle, vf_tokens.t27, the Outfit raster face (vf_type) and petal_menu_wasm.t27 exist only in
;     open PR 13254 (T27F-007); vf_scale exists only in open PR 13250.
;   - display_list.t27 flattens a scene.t27 Scene (32 nodes, 128 ops), not a VfGraph; vf_render.t27
;     paints a VfGraph straight to RGB and skips the list. DL_PATH carries 4 ints, too few for a quad,
;     and DL_TEXT carries no glyph.
;   - frame_render.t27 is the shared integer raster: it draws rect, fill, opacity and group, and
;     refuses path, stroke and text.
;   - glass_window.t27 (desktop) and petal_framebuffer.t27 (fpga) both draw from petal_menu.t27
;     directly; neither plays a display list. hdmi_timing_640x480.t27 and tmds_encoder.t27 exist; the
;     board top and the HDMI pin table in fpga/HARDWARE_SSOT.md do not.
; --
; Order (UT_STEP_*): the menu on the desktop first, because its host is on master and its player waits
; on no open PR; then the browser, which waits on PR 13254 and on t27b wasm body lowering; then the
; FPGA, which waits on a board top and the HDMI pins; then the UI Kit on all three, which waits on
; VcStyle (PR 13254).
; --
; Style law of the menu, the same on every target: background 0x000000, text 0xFFFFFF, the Outfit face,
; 27 petals lettered A..Z and Ti as petal_menu.t27 spells them. Letters and colours never move between
; targets. A frosted hover in white reads white, not grey; a tinted frost keeps at least 7.6:1 contrast
; over black. The contrast rule is a plan constant here because no spec checks it yet (arrow A4).
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN), integer only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module t27f_ui_targets;

